I disagree that Lichs are cool pets.  First of all, they are quite
dangerous, I still have some unexplained deaths resulting from confused
lich pets.  If you want to keep a lich as a pet make sure it has a
unicorn horn otherwise it beats on you and if you try to run it will
teleport to you.  Another problem is that they use a cold attack and it
can take a lot of keystrokes and animation to cycle through monsters
getting mildly chilly from them.  Also, if a Lich goes feral but
peaceful it will still continue to teleport to you but without the
benefit of you being able to displace it.  Mindflayers are also not
worth the benefit, IMO.

However, in general I agree strongly that using a poly trap for strong
pets is a great tool and I rely on it heavily.  I prefer carnivores so
that I can keep on feeding them and increase their tameness.  Umber
Hulk digging teams are useful, too.

Another benefit of strong pets is that there is someone there to
protect you if you run into a floating eye, etc.



